// src/v4/std/logic.dag
//
// Scope: classical two-valued logic — the `Bool` truth value and its
//        algebraic grounding. The boolean kernel every predicate returns.
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boolean_algebra
//         (two-element / classical bivalent logic; the Boolean data type)
//
// Owns:
//   - Bool — the closed two-variant truth value (a `Disj` of True | False)
//   - inhabitance: Bool inhabits `BooleanAlgebra` (std/algebra.dag) —
//     conjunction / disjunction / negation FALL OUT of the algebra; they
//     are never re-declared here (epistemic stacking)
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag: Disj
//   - std/algebra.dag: BooleanAlgebra
//
// Status: T-3 logic modeled 2026-05-16 (still-fox-366). The I/O contract
//   in this header is immutable for downstream workers. Splitting this
//   file requires explicit operator ratification (substrate extension =
//   stop signal).
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.std.logic


import v4.std.algebra { BooleanAlgebra, BoundedLattice, Lattice }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// `Bool` is kernel-ambient (provided by the v2 seed, usable without an
// import — STRUCTURE.md "Kernel-ambient types"). That relaxes only the
// import edge: this file remains `Bool`'s SOLE modeling authority. The
// v4 model of `Bool` is the closed two-variant `Disj` declared below.
//
// INHABITANCE IS AN INSTANCE-VALUE, NOT A KEYWORD (operator-ratified).
// `Bool` inhabits `BooleanAlgebra` by the `data bool_boolean_algebra`
// declaration below — a real `BooleanAlgebra<Bool>` value in THIS file.
// There is no `inhabits` keyword and no inhabitance carrier; the relation
// IS the instance value. The boolean operations — conjunction (meet),
// disjunction (join), negation (complement), the constants top/bottom —
// are NOT re-declared as free functions here (the v3 mistake: see
// dsl/std/logic.dag's free `classical_and`/`classical_or`/`classical_not`,
// a parallel authority disjoint from the algebra). They FALL OUT of the
// instance by walking it: `bool_boolean_algebra.complement` IS negation,
// `bool_boolean_algebra.bounded_lattice.lattice.meet` IS conjunction.
// One authority per operation (INVARIANTS P2); epistemic stacking
// (THESIS) — `Bool`'s logic is GROUNDED in the algebra, not asserted
// alongside it.
//
// LAWS ARE GROUNDED DEFINITIONS, NOT FIELDS. The Boolean-algebra axioms
// (complement: meet(a,complement(a))==bottom, join(a,complement(a))==top;
// distributivity; the bounded-lattice absorption/identity laws) ARE the
// definition of the named structure `BooleanAlgebra` (algebra.dag,
// anchored to Wikipedia "Boolean algebra (structure)"). They are not
// stored as a flag and not hand-built equation ASTs here; the L7
// algebra-law surface (lens/coverage.dag + lens/testgen.dag) derives the
// per-axiom TestClaim corpus from that cited definition.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Bool — the classical two-valued truth value: the `Disj` of True|False.
//
// The codomain of every predicate and the carrier classical
// `BooleanAlgebra` is defined over. Bivalent by construction — exactly
// two values, no third (law of excluded middle ∧ non-contradiction).
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: True/False are not per-consumer scattered
//      facts; every predicate, every `Branch`, every boolean fold
//      handles BOTH (the two outcomes of every decision). No consumer
//      uses only one variant.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the two variants are nullary and carry
//      no payload — there is no uniform label space to fold to. Promoting
//      to `{ bit: Int }` replaces a closed 2-valued exhaustive sum with
//      an unbounded Int (`bit=42` representable) — violates INVARIANTS P2
//      + M4 (closed sets are enums, not numeric proxies). The 2-variant
//      enum IS the faithful form.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A by construction: `Bool` IS the carrier
//      classical `BooleanAlgebra` is defined over and the std/ ground
//      other logic attaches to; there is no richer std/ source to trace
//      to — pointing it elsewhere is circular.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a truth value is EXACTLY ONE of True/False
//      (bivalence — excluded middle ∧ non-contradiction); mutually-
//      exclusive alternatives, never simultaneous coordinates. No value
//      is "both".
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: True/False are two nullary
//      constructors — there is no source set X they project over, no
//      generic `F<X>` (Practice 7). The 2-element set IS a projection
//      source, not a projection of one; no enumeration-to-projection
//      collapse exists.
// Terminal: the irreducible two-element inductive definition of the
// classical truth value; the carrier classical Boolean algebra grounds in.
type Bool = True | False


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// bool_boolean_algebra — Bool's inhabitance of `BooleanAlgebra` (the
// operator-ratified instance-value form: a real `BooleanAlgebra<Bool>`
// value declared in this file).
//
// Walking the instance yields every boolean operation, one authority each:
//   - bounded_lattice.lattice.meet   — conjunction (AND)
//   - bounded_lattice.lattice.join   — disjunction (OR)
//   - bounded_lattice.top            — the True constant (meet identity)
//   - bounded_lattice.bottom         — the False constant (join identity)
//   - complement                     — negation (NOT)
//
// `meet`/`join`/`complement` are the standard two-valued truth tables;
// each is total over the closed `Bool` Disj (both variants covered, no
// fail-open arm). The Boolean-algebra axioms they satisfy are the
// grounded definition of `BooleanAlgebra` (see Modeling notes), not
// asserted here.
data bool_boolean_algebra: BooleanAlgebra<Bool> = BooleanAlgebra {
  bounded_lattice: BoundedLattice {
    lattice: Lattice {
      meet: fn(a, b) {
        match a {
          True => b
          False => False
        }
      },
      join: fn(a, b) {
        match a {
          True => True
          False => b
        }
      }
    },
    top: True,
    bottom: False
  },
  complement: fn(a) {
    match a {
      True => False
      False => True
    }
  }
}
